  "query_preview": "..\n/Issued 507 AM MDT Fri Jul 24 2026/ \n\nUpper-level ridging will continue across the Intermountain West\nkeeping Montana hot for at least a while. High temperatures \nranging from the upper 90s to mid 100s are expected across the \nlower elevations through Sunday with poor overnight temperature \nrecovery expected for portions of North-Central Montana \nhighlighted in the Extreme Heat Warning. Those recreating or\nspending an extended amount of time outdoors should prepare to\ntake plenty of breaks, stay hydrated, and be on the lookout for\nany symptoms of heat-related illness.\n\nAdditionally there will be daily chances for isolated to scattered\nafternoon thunderstorms over the next few days. Thunderstorms on\nFriday and Saturday are expected to be on the drier side which \nmeans there will be a concern that cloud to ground lightning and \ngusty, erratic winds may further increase already present fire \nweather concerns.\n\nWhile the worst of the heat is expected to be over after Sunday,\nit may be a while before a true cool down is expected as long-\nrange models suggest the upper-level ridge could persist through\nat least the end of next week. Those who are most sensitive to the\nheat should be on the lookout for compounding heat stress,\nespecially if they are without air conditioning or unable to find\na cool location to recover. -thor",
